---
import Icon from '~/components/Icon.astro';
---

<section id="difference" class="py-12 md:py-16 lg:py-20 border-y border-border/40 bg-surface/24">
  <div class="container-app">
    <div class="max-w-3xl reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow"><Icon name="chart" size={14} /> What category this is</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4">We do not sell strategies. We host yours.</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-fluid-lg text-muted">
        That distinction matters. The site should not read like a subscription EA pitch or a promise of edge. Glitch Trade is infrastructure for user-authored trading automation: simple enough for a quick rule, deep enough for a coded strategy and a prop-firm-aware dashboard.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr_1fr_1.1fr] bg-surface-2/70 text-fluid-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-subtle">
        <div class="px-4 py-3">Comparison</div>
        <div class="px-4 py-3">TradingView only</div>
        <div class="px-4 py-3">Broker-native only</div>
        <div class="px-4 py-3">Glitch Trade</div>
      </div>
      {[
        ['Execution', 'Alerts and charting, no hosted execution path', 'One broker, one account view', 'Run rules across supported broker paths with one marketing and tracking model'],
        ['Backtesting', 'Depends on your own setup', 'Usually limited or broker-specific', 'Built into the platform with optional Firm Mode guardrails'],
        ['Tracking', 'Separate from execution', 'Single-broker dashboard', 'Universal multi-account dashboard with per-bot attribution'],
        ['Prop challenges', 'No native challenge tracking', 'Rarely challenge-aware', 'Firm Mode for FundingPips, FTMO, MFF, Apex, The5ers'],
      ].map((row) => (
        <div class="grid grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr_1fr_1.1fr] border-t border-border/60 bg-bg/55 text-fluid-sm">
          <div class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold text-fg">{row[0]}</div>
          <div class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">{row[1]}</div>
          <div class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">{row[2]}</div>
          <div class="px-4 py-4 text-fg/90">{row[3]}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
